From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jinbo Zhang <jinboz1@uci.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:21:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] track_building: match reconstructed tracks on
 hit_id[track_edges]

load_reconstruction_df used graph.track_edges (node indices) as if they
were hit ids. Whenever node-level hard_cuts removed hits, every particle
was attached to the wrong hits: connected components on the truth graph
scored 0.000 efficiency on a hard-cut TrackML event (should be 1.000).

gd-displaced patch 0001 (plan item a).
---
 acorn/stages/track_building/utils.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/acorn/stages/track_building/utils.py b/acorn/stages/track_building/utils.py
index afec1763..531a5e1f 100644
--- a/acorn/stages/track_building/utils.py
+++ b/acorn/stages/track_building/utils.py
@@ -38,7 +38,9 @@ def load_reconstruction_df(graph):
 
     reco_df = pd.DataFrame({"hit_id": hit_id, "track_id": graph.hit_track_labels})
 
-    node_id = graph.track_edges.reshape(-1)
+    # track_edges hold node indices, not hit ids. They only coincide when no
+    # node-level cut (e.g. hard_cuts) has been applied, so map through hit_id.
+    node_id = hit_id[graph.track_edges.reshape(-1)]
     pids = graph.track_particle_id.repeat(2)
     pid_df = pd.DataFrame({"hit_id": node_id, "particle_id": pids})
     pid_df.drop_duplicates(subset=["hit_id", "particle_id"], inplace=True)
